tary/Border Patrol operation did result in arrests in June.\\nBut today, the State of Texas moved in with force to reclaim control of the island from the cartels:\\nAccording to a post by Governor Greg Abbott on x.com (Twitter) one of the first things the state did was to literally plant the Texas flag on Fronton Island to make it plainly clear who was in charge:\\n\\"This is OUR land. We\'ve taken control of it away from transnational criminal organizations that were using it to facilitate illegal immigration & drug smuggling. Thanks to @TxDPS & @TexasGuard. Plant the Texas flag.\\"-Texas Governor Greg Abbott on x.com (Twitter)\\nIncidentally, today\'s operation wasn\'t a \\"one-off.\\" Texas Land Commissioner Dr. Dawn Buckingham has also declared two smaller islands (totalling more than 45 acres) on the Rio Grande in Maverick County near Eagle Pass to be Texas State Property which gives the DPS law enforcement authority there.\\nWhat are your thoughts about today\'s operation by the State of Texas on the Rio Grande?\\nShare your opinions in the comments to this article.\\nWant more stories like this? Be sure to \\"like\\" this article and follow me on theNewsbreak app!\\nOther stories by Jack Beaversabout Texas Border issues include:\\nMigrants Plant Foreign Flag on Texas Soil\\nU.S. Soldiers vs. Mexican Cartels? Support for Military Action Grows\\nCartels Shot Texans in Mexico by \\"Mistake\\"\\nMake Money Writing For Newsbreak!APPLY HERE","answer":"The Texas Department of Public Safety (DPS) has taken control of Fronton Island in the Rio Grande, which has been a hotspot for Mexican cartel smuggling activities. The island, known for its heavy vegetation, has served as a hiding and staging area for cartel operations. The DPS, with the help of surveillance cameras, has been monitoring armed cartel members on the island. In August, Border Patrol Agents discovered automatic weapons and ammunition during a cartel gunrunning operation on Fronton Island. The State of Texas has now reclaimed control of the island and planted the Texas flag to assert its authority. Additionally, two smaller islands near Eagle Pass have been declared Texas State Property, granting the DPS law enforcement authority there.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":210},{"index":1,"byte_start":210,"byte_end":340},{"index":2,"byte_start":340,"byte_end":508},{"index":3,"byte_start":508,"byte_end":627},{"index":4,"byte_start":627,"byte_end":775},{"index":5,"byte_start":775,"byte_end":920},{"index":6,"byte_start":920,"byte_end":1067},{"index":7,"byte_start":1067,"byte_end":1249},{"index":8,"byte_start":1249,"byte_end":1570},{"index":9,"byte_start":1570,"byte_end":1714},{"index":10,"byte_start":1714,"byte_end":1746},{"index":11,"byte_start":1746,"byte_end":1867},{"index":12,"byte_start":1867,"byte_end":2113},{"index":13,"byte_start":2113,"byte_end":2201},{"index":14,"byte_start":2201,"byte_end":2254},{"index":15,"byte_start":2254,"byte_end":2283},{"index":16,"byte_start":2283,"byte_end":2349},{"index":17,"byte_start":2349,"byte_end":2490},{"index":18,"byte_start":2490,"byte_end":2610}],"answer_sentence_indices":[0,1,2,3,4,5],"answer_offsets":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":165},{"index":1,"byte_start":165,"byte_end":272},{"index":2,"byte_start":272,"byte_end":376},{"index":3,"byte_start":376,"byte_end":508},{"index":4,"byte_start":508,"byte_end":619},{"index":5,"byte_start":619,"byte_end":759}]}', 'request_index': 0, 'sentence_indices': [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 'token_count_measured': True}, 'response': {'choices': [{'finish_reason': 'stop', 'index': 0, 'message': {'content': '0|E|0.95|[0,1]\n1|E|0.95|[2]\n2|E|0.95|[1,4]\n3|E|0.95|[3]\n4|E|0.95|[6,7]\n5|E|0.95|[8]', 'role': 'assistant'}}], 'created': 1791259411, 'id': 'chatcmpl-LV5PcOo9f1qgOCTUjxeL0ve1fq0BFOKf', 'model': 'unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF', 'object': 'chat.completion', 'system_fingerprint': 'b9606-9b4dae81f', 'timings': {'cache_n': 0, 'predicted_ms': 2069.976, 'predicted_n': 84, 'pred