e same time the issue is gaining momentum.\\" Conservative groups were vocal in their opposition, with one, known as the Network Pushing for Normalization of Education, telling the Japan Times that granting same-sex couples the same rights as all other Japanese citizens would degrade the \\"familial system and practice that heterosexual unions have long preserved in human history.\\" While Shibuya\'s registration system will be a first for Japan, Yodogawa ward in the western Japanese city of Osaka was the first in the nation to recognize and support the LGBT community. In 2013 the ward government pledged to give consideration to the issues that the community faced, and to train staff to accommodate needs specific to LGBT individuals. Journalist Chie Kobayashi contributed reporting from Tokyo.\\n","answer":"The government of Shibuya ward in Tokyo, Japan has passed an ordinance allowing for \\"partnership certificates\\" for same-sex couples. This move allows registered same-sex partners in Shibuya to have visitation rights in hospitals and co-sign tenancy agreements. While these certificates are not legally binding and do not grant all the advantages enjoyed by heterosexual married couples, proponents of marriage equality see it as a step in the right direction. The hope is that this decision will promote marriage equality for the gay community and increase visibility and understanding of LGBT issues. Taiga Ishikawa, the first openly gay local assembly member in Japan, called it a \\"big first step for the protection of human rights.\\" However, he emphasized the importance of education about alternative lifestyles. Neighboring Setagaya ward has shown interest in following Shibuya\'s lead, but Ishikawa cautions that a national law is needed to achieve equal rights for gay couples. While discrimination against the LGBT community is not widespread in Japan, many individuals still hide their sexuality due to societal pressures. A recent poll found that a majority oppose gay marriage, but support is higher among young adults.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":133},{"index":1,"byte_start":133,"byte_end":407},{"index":2,"byte_start":407,"byte_end":560},{"index":3,"byte_start":560,"byte_end":746},{"index":4,"byte_start":746,"byte_end":823},{"index":5,"byte_start":823,"byte_end":1046},{"index":6,"byte_start":1046,"byte_end":1187},{"index":7,"byte_start":1187,"byte_end":1359},{"index":8,"byte_start":1359,"byte_end":1518},{"index":9,"byte_start":1518,"byte_end":1633},{"index":10,"byte_start":1633,"byte_end":1803},{"index":11,"byte_start":1803,"byte_end":1909},{"index":12,"byte_start":1909,"byte_end":2155},{"index":13,"byte_start":2155,"byte_end":2245},{"index":14,"byte_start":2245,"byte_end":2342},{"index":15,"byte_start":2342,"byte_end":2425},{"index":16,"byte_start":2425,"byte_end":2582},{"index":17,"byte_start":2582,"byte_end":2664},{"index":18,"byte_start":2664,"byte_end":2693},{"index":19,"byte_start":2693,"byte_end":2839},{"index":20,"byte_start":2839,"byte_end":2992},{"index":21,"byte_start":2992,"byte_end":3215},{"index":22,"byte_start":3215,"byte_end":3362},{"index":23,"byte_start":3362,"byte_end":3530},{"index":24,"byte_start":3530,"byte_end":3867},{"index":25,"byte_start":3867,"byte_end":4055},{"index":26,"byte_start":4055,"byte_end":4223},{"index":27,"byte_start":4223,"byte_end":4283}],"answer_sentence_indices":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"answer_offsets":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":133},{"index":1,"byte_start":133,"byte_end":261},{"index":2,"byte_start":261,"byte_end":460},{"index":3,"byte_start":460,"byte_end":602},{"index":4,"byte_start":602,"byte_end":736},{"index":5,"byte_start":736,"byte_end":817},{"index":6,"byte_start":817,"byte_end":984},{"index":7,"byte_start":984,"byte_end":1131},{"index":8,"byte_start":1131,"byte_end":1229}]}', 'request_index': 0, 'sentence_indices': [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], 'token_count_measured': True}, 'response': {'choices': [{'finish_reason': 'stop', 'index': 0, 'messa