ite and gin took their turns dancing on my tongue and the result was tremendous. I got a taste of the Oaxacanut and a mystery Holiday Special and those were both also to die for.\\\\n\\\\nThere are also plenty of food options in the area if the bar nuts that Donald and the crew serve don\'t sate your hunger.\\\\n\\\\nCould not throw enough support behind this business. Get there already!\\"}],\\"state\\":\\"CA\\"}","answer":"The Imperial is a local bar located at 320 S Kellogg Ave in Goleta, CA. It falls under the categories of Arts & Entertainment, Jazz & Blues, Lounges, Nightlife, Bars, and Cocktail Bars. The bar has specific operating hours, opening at 5:00 PM from Wednesday to Saturday. The business does not take reservations and offers outdoor seating. WiFi is not available, but the bar is known for its relaxed and cozy atmosphere. \\n\\nAccording to customer reviews, The Imperial has received a high rating of 4.5 stars. One customer expressed their excitement that the bar survived the challenges posed by Covid-19 and praised its speakeasy vibe. They highlighted the friendly staff, strong drinks, and great music selection. Another customer had a less positive experience, mentioning that the bartenders did not provide satisfactory service and lacked gratitude towards patrons. \\n\\nThe bar\'s ambience is described as classy and intimate, with a distinct speakeasy vibe. It is located at the back of a bike shop, giving it a hidden feel. The decor is impressive, with a notable vinyl collection and suitable lighting and furniture. The outdoor area offers additional space and visual diversions. Customers also mentioned the delicious cocktails, such as the Clover Club, Oaxacanut, and a mystery Holiday Special. The Imperial is highly recommended by customers, with one stating that it deserves its five-star reviews.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":841},{"index":1,"byte_start":841,"byte_end":889},{"index":2,"byte_start":889,"byte_end":998},{"inde