ount in Windows 10, you can use this account to log on to your PC. You are allowed to recover Windows 10 password free from command prompt. But if you are the only user of your computer, skip to get Windows 10 password finder.f you have another admin account in Windows 10, you can use this account to log on to your PC. You are allowed to recover Windows 10 password free from command prompt. But if you are the only user of your computer, skip to get Windows 10 password finder.\\\\n\\\\n\\",\\"question\\":\\"how to determine administrators on windows 10\\"}","answer":"Based on the given passages, here\'s how to determine administrators on Windows 10:\\n\\n1. Enable the built-in administrator account:\\n\\t* Open elevated Command Prompt (Press Windows key + R, type \\"cmd\\", and press Ctrl + Shift + Enter).\\n\\t* Type \\"net user administrator /enable\\" and press Enter.\\n\\t* Uncheck the option labeled \\"Account is disabled\\" in the Properties dialog.\\n\\t* Click Apply and close the Local Users and Groups window.\\n2. Use another admin account:\\n\\t* If there\'s another admin account on the computer, use it to log in.\\n\\t* If there\'s no other admin account, skip to using a Windows 10 password finder.\\n\\nSo, to determine administrators on Windows 10, you can either enable the built-in administrator account or use another existing admin account.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":153},{"index":1,"byte_start":153,"byte_end":486},{"index":2,"byte_start":486,"byte_end":632},{"index":3,"byte_start":632,"byte_end":645},{"index":4,"byte_start":645,"byte_end":827},{"index":5,"byte_start":827,"byte_end":1066},{"index":6,"byte_start":1066,"byte_end":1288},{"index":7,"byte_start":1288,"byte_end":1361},{"index":8,"byte_start":1361,"byte_end":1542},{"index":9,"byte_start":1542,"byte_end":1615},{"index":10,"byte_start":1615,"byte_end":1766}],"answer_sentence_indices":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6],"answer_offsets":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":232},{"index