o calzone was average and nothing special. \\\\n\\\\nSeating was awkward, but nice that it was outdoors.\\"},{\\"review_date\\":\\"2012-03-28 00:16:21\\",\\"review_stars\\":1.0,\\"review_text\\":\\"Pasta house is the lowest of the low. First of all, pasta is one of the cheapest foods for a restaurant to prepare fresh. But at Pasta House, everything is frozen. Can\'t tell you how many times I\'ve taken home a baked ziti that was rock hard and cold in the middle. And because it isn\'t fresh, the pasta doesn\'t really seem to hold up as leftovers in the fridge, usually getting soggy and inedible. \\\\n\\\\nBut wait, there\'s more! The pricing is just unacceptable, $8-$10 (or more) for one medium-sized serving of pasta which is never a notch above barely mediocre. You are seriously better off buying the ingredients and making it yourself  - it\'ll cost roughly the same and it\'ll be fresh, and the cashier won\'t shamelessly hit on you in an attempt to haggle for tips.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, did I mention that they take forever? That\'s because they put their frozen iced pasta blocks in the oven to give the impression that it\'s being cooked fresh. Pasta House, you ain\'t foolin\' nobody. Put it in the damn microwave and save us the dramatics. Or better yet, just make it fresh.\\"},{\\"review_date\\":\\"2011-11-15 17:37:42\\",\\"review_stars\\":1.0,\\"review_text\\":\\"Pasta House disappointed--long wait 20-30 minutes & very sub par food--very spicy marinara, & bland veggies. A decent portion for the price, but i\'d rather get a small amount of good than a large amount of mediocre bordering on bad..let\'s just say I could have done better myself. But I did like the garlic bread.\\"}],\\"state\\":\\"CA\\"}","answer":"Pasta House, located at 6546 Pardall Rd, Goleta, CA, is an Italian restaurant that does not take reservations and offers outdoor seating and takeout services. The restaurant, which opens at unspecified hours, is good for groups but does not offer WiFi, music, or any specific ambience. According to customer reviews, the Pasta House has an average rating of 3 stars. Some customers have raised concerns about the quality of the food, stating that the pasta appears to be frozen and reheated, resulting in less-than-ideal texture and taste. Others have criticized the long wait times and the high prices for the mediocre quality of the dishes. Positive comments include the availability of outdoor seating and the decent portion sizes.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":655},{"index":1,"byte_start":655,"byte_end":668},{"index":2,"byte_start":668,"byte_end":802},{"index":3,"byte_start":802,"byte_end":969},{"index":4,"byte_start":969,"byte_end":1053},{"index":5,"byte_start":1053,"byte_end":1095},{"index":6,"byte_start":1095,"byte_end":1197},{"index":7,"byte_start":1197,"byte_end":1330},{"index":8,"byte_start":1330,"byte_end":1358},{"index":9,"byte_start":1358,"byte_end":1493},{"index":10,"byte_start":1493,"byte_end":1745},{"index":11,"byte_start":1745,"byte_end":1865},{"index":12,"byte_start":1865,"byte_end":1904},{"index":13,"byte_start":1904,"byte_end":1960},{"index":14,"byte_start":1960,"byte_end":2177},{"index":15,"byte_start":2177,"byte_end":2349},{"index":16,"byte_start":2349,"byte_end":2398}],"answer_sentence_indices":[0,1,2,3,4,5],"answer_offsets":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":159},{"index":1,"byte_start":159,"byte_end":286},{"index":2,"byte_start":286,"byte_end":367},{"index":3,"byte_start":367,"byte_end":540},{"index":4,"byte_start":540,"byte_end":643},{"index":5,"byte_start":643,"byte_end":734}]}', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF', 'seed': 70781, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0}, 'rendered_input_tokens': 1336, 'rendered_prompt': '<|im_start|>user\n{"instruction":"For each requested answer sentence emit index|E/C/B|p_unsupported with two decimals|[zero to two source segment indices]. One record per line in input order; no other text. Relations and addresses are predictions.","so