ing time.richloroacetic Acid Peel (TCA). The TCA peel causes a second degree burn on the epidermis and upper portion of the dermis, which means it will take longer to heal than a superficial peel. Following the procedure the skin will begin to crust and peel in the first 2-3 days.\\\\n\\\\n\\",\\"question\\":\\"how long does it take to heal from a chemical peel\\"}","answer":"Based on the given passages, the healing time for a chemical peel can range from 1 to 14 days, depending on the depth of the peel. A deep peel can take between 10 to 14 days for skin regrowth, with the skin remaining red for up to 3 weeks or even 2 months for some individuals. Most people take about 2 weeks off from work.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":110},{"index":1,"byte_start":110,"byte_end":317},{"index":2,"byte_start":317,"byte_end":375},{"index":3,"byte_start":375,"byte_end":436},{"index":4,"byte_start":436,"byte_end":512},{"index":5,"byte_start":512,"byte_end":593},{"index":6,"byte_start":593,"byte_end":775},{"index":7,"byte_start":775,"byte_end":941},{"index":8,"byte_start":941,"byte_end":1097},{"index":9,"byte_start":1097,"byte_end":1185},{"index":10,"byte_start":1185,"byte_end":1452},{"index":11,"byte_start":1452,"byte_end":1608},{"index":12,"byte_start":1608,"byte_end":1762}],"answer_sentence_indices":[0,1,2],"answer_offsets":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":131},{"index":1,"byte_start":131,"byte_end":278},{"index":2,"byte_start":278,"byte_end":323}]}', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF', 'seed': 70781, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0}, 'rendered_input_tokens': 870, 'rendered_prompt': '<|im_start|>user\n{"instruction":"For each requested answer sentence emit index|E/C/B|p_unsupported with two decimals|[zero to two source segment indices]. One record per line in input order; no other text. Relations and addresses are predictions.","source":"{\\"passages\\":\\"passage 1:In a chemical peel, a chemical solution is applied to the skin a