se to be bigger. The guy that wrapped my sandwich must be new or something because he did not make the sandwich nicely (most ingrediants were on the wrapper and he also didn\'t wrap the sandwich correctly. Everything was falling out of it. I normally like all the Subway\'s I go to, but the one on Milpas needs to be less greedy when it comes to the serving amount of tuna, like I said before, there was hardly any tuna on the sandwich and also better at putting the sandwich together. I most likely won\'t go back to this Subway.\\"}],\\"state\\":\\"CA\\"}","answer":"Subway, located at 609 N Milpas St, Santa Barbara, CA, offers a range of options including sandwiches, fast food, breakfast and brunch. The store is open every day of the week, with slightly reduced hours on Sunday. Features include outdoor seating and takeout options, with no WiFi and no reservations required. The restaurant is suitable for groups. The business has received an average rating of 2.5 stars.\\n\\nHowever, customer reviews have expressed dissatisfaction with the service. One customer reported a negative experience with an employee\'s attitude and inability to correctly prepare a sandwich. Another customer was distressed by employees not wearing masks properly during the COVID-19 pandemic and one employee was seen wiping his face frequently. A third customer complained about the insufficient quantity of tuna in their sandwich and issues with sandwich assembly. These experiences have reflected poorly on this Subway location.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":815},{"index":1,"byte_start":815,"byte_end":888},{"index":2,"byte_start":888,"byte_end":1007},{"index":3,"byte_start":1007,"byte_end":1064},{"index":4,"byte_start":1064,"byte_end":1189},{"index":5,"byte_start":1189,"byte_end":1314},{"index":6,"byte_start":1314,"byte_end":1466},{"index":7,"byte_start":1466,"byte_end":1513},{"index":8,"byte_start":1513,"byte_end":1606},{"index":9,"byte_start":1606,"byte_end":1648},{"index