ate needs specific to LGBT individuals. Journalist Chie Kobayashi contributed reporting from Tokyo.\\n","answer":"The government of Shibuya ward in Tokyo, Japan has passed an ordinance allowing for \\"partnership certificates\\" for same-sex couples. This move allows registered same-sex partners in Shibuya to have visitation rights in hospitals and co-sign tenancy agreements. While these certificates are not legally binding and do not grant all the advantages enjoyed by heterosexual married couples, proponents of marriage equality see it as a step in the right direction. The hope is that this decision will promote marriage equality for the gay community and increase visibility and understanding of LGBT issues. Taiga Ishikawa, the first openly gay local assembly member in Japan, called it a \\"big first step for the protection of human rights.\\" However, he emphasized the importance of education about alternative lifestyles. Neighboring Setagaya ward has shown interest in following Shibuya\'s lead, but Ishikawa cautions that a national law is needed to achieve equal rights for gay couples. While discrimination against the LGBT community is not widespread in Japan, many individuals still hide their sexuality due to societal pressures. A recent poll found that a majority oppose gay marriage, but support is higher among young adults.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":133},{"index":1,"byte_start":133,"byte_end":407},{"index":2,"byte_start":407,"byte_end":560},{"index":3,"byte_start":560,"byte_end":746},{"index":4,"byte_start":746,"byte_end":823},{"index":5,"byte_start":823,"byte_end":1046},{"index":6,"byte_start":1046,"byte_end":1187},{"index":7,"byte_start":1187,"byte_end":1359},{"index":8,"byte_start":1359,"byte_end":1518},{"index":9,"byte_start":1518,"byte_end":1633},{"index":10,"byte_start":1633,"byte_end":1803},{"index":11,"byte_start":1803,"byte_end":1909},{"index":12,"byte_start":1909,"byte_end":2155},{"index":13,"byte_start":2155,"byte_end