he nail polish remover cap, place the applicator over the opening, and invert the bottle to soak it. Alternatively, you could pour the nail polish remover into a bowl and dip the cotton ball or paper towel into the solution.\\\\n\\\\n\\",\\"question\\":\\"remove nail polish without polish remover\\"}","answer":"Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to remove nail polish without using a polish remover:\\n\\n1. Soaking your hands in warm soap water for 2-3 minutes to remove the spray (Passage 1)\\n2. Scratching the nail polish lightly and pulling it off (Passage 1)\\n3. Using Q-tips as an alternative to cotton swabs (Passage 1)\\n4. Applying lemon juice to the nails and letting it sit for a few minutes before removing the polish (Passage 2)\\n5. Using an emery board to gently scrape off the nail polish (Passage 2)\\n\\nIt\'s important to note that these methods may not be as effective or efficient as using a traditional nail polish remover, and they may not completely remove all traces of the polish.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":98},{"index":1,"byte_start":98,"byte_end":172},{"index":2,"byte_start":172,"byte_end":261},{"index":3,"byte_start":261,"byte_end":313},{"index":4,"byte_start":313,"byte_end":457},{"index":5,"byte_start":457,"byte_end":553},{"index":6,"byte_start":553,"byte_end":607},{"index":7,"byte_start":607,"byte_end":744},{"index":8,"byte_start":744,"byte_end":1023},{"index":9,"byte_start":1023,"byte_end":1088},{"index":10,"byte_start":1088,"byte_end":1158},{"index":11,"byte_start":1158,"byte_end":1312},{"index":12,"byte_start":1312,"byte_end":1389},{"index":13,"byte_start":1389,"byte_end":1485},{"index":14,"byte_start":1485,"byte_end":1581},{"index":15,"byte_start":1581,"byte_end":1632},{"index":16,"byte_start":1632,"byte_end":1742},{"index":17,"byte_start":1742,"byte_end":1926}],"answer_sentence_indices":[0],"answer_offsets":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":696}]}', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'unsloth/Qwen3.8