g security around places of worship, “The Farmington Hills Police Department has been fielding numerous calls from community members expressing concern for their personal safety and the safety of others as the conflict in the Middle East continues to grow,” the city said in a statement.\\nFarmington Hills Police Chief Jeff King has said that after speaking with state and federal intelligence partners there does not seem to be a credible threat at this time.\\nThat said, police will make a visible presence at places of worship and schools.","answer":"Jewish groups in Michigan are on high alert following a call for Muslim protests by a former high-ranking Hamas member, Khalid Meshaal, in support of Palestinians in the Gaza Strip. Israel has locked down the Gaza Strip following a recent attack by Hamas. The Jewish Federation of Metropolitan Detroit has stated there are no specific or credible threats at this time. Farmington Hills Police Department will increase security around places of worship and schools despite there being no credible threat.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":216},{"index":1,"byte_start":216,"byte_end":319},{"index":2,"byte_start":319,"byte_end":351},{"index":3,"byte_start":351,"byte_end":426},{"index":4,"byte_start":426,"byte_end":552},{"index":5,"byte_start":552,"byte_end":645},{"index":6,"byte_start":645,"byte_end":705},{"index":7,"byte_start":705,"byte_end":773},{"index":8,"byte_start":773,"byte_end":899},{"index":9,"byte_start":899,"byte_end":1003},{"index":10,"byte_start":1003,"byte_end":1183},{"index":11,"byte_start":1183,"byte_end":1401},{"index":12,"byte_start":1401,"byte_end":1761},{"index":13,"byte_start":1761,"byte_end":1933},{"index":14,"byte_start":1933,"byte_end":2013}],"answer_sentence_indices":[0,1,2,3],"answer_offsets":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":182},{"index":1,"byte_start":182,"byte_end":256},{"index":2,"byte_start":256,"byte_end":369},{"index":3,"byte_start":369,"byte_end":503}]}', 'role': 'user