ied any such orders being issued and said the men deserted. ISIS released videos that showed what seemed to be an endless line of military recruits marched at gunpoint and later posted images showing cold-blooded mass killings. Damon said Iraqi officials told her it may take weeks or months to exhume all the bodies. Human Rights Watch described the \\"Speicher Massacre\\" -- as it has been dubbed in Iraq -- as the \\"largest reported incident\\" where \\"ISIS captured more than 1,000 soldiers fleeing Camp Speicher ... then summarily executed at least 800 of them.\\" Based on satellite imagery and witness testimony, Human Rights Watch last year was able to identity a number of mass grave sites inside Tikrit and the presidential palace complex. The families gave DNA samples to the Iraqi Ministry of Health last year so authorities would be able to match them to unidentified bodies the government may find. CNN\'s Arwa Damon reported from Tikrit, and Ralph Ellis wrote in Atlanta. CNN\'s Jomana Karadsheh contributed to this report.\\n","answer":"Eleven mass graves, believed to contain up to 1,700 bodies, have been discovered in newly liberated Tikrit. The bodies are thought to be Iraqi soldiers, who ISIS claimed to have executed in June last year. The bodies were decomposed, some with their hands bound. 47 bodies have been exhumed so far from two of the graves, and will be sent to Baghdad for DNA testing. There may be eight more graves inside the presidential palace complex, which was ISIS headquarters after the militants occupied the city. The bodies are believed to have been of soldiers fleeing from Camp Speicher, a fortified Iraqi base near Tikrit.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":110},{"index":1,"byte_start":110,"byte_end":147},{"index":2,"byte_start":147,"byte_end":272},{"index":3,"byte_start":272,"byte_end":407},{"index":4,"byte_start":407,"byte_end":564},{"index":5,"byte_start":564,"byte_end":675},{"index":6,"byte_start":675,"byte_end":727},