ians, who took to Twitter to voice their displeasure. Adam Bond, a British actor of mixed heritage, including Native American, portrays Jesus during the historical reenactments in \\"Finding Jesus.\\" And Juan Pablo Di Pace -- a Argentinian named after the late St. Pope John Paul II -- takes a starring role in \\"A.D.,\\" replacing Diogo Morgado, dubbed \\"hot Jesus,\\" by some, \\"smarmy Jesus\\" by others. You could make the case that authenticity is the coin of our current entertainment realm, and that filmmakers are competing to make their work as historically accurate as possible. Contemporary viewers are too savvy to stomach the fake beards and odd accents that littered the camels-and-sandals epics of eras past. But there\'s another, deeper meaning behind our new, multicultural Jesuses, scholars say. \\"Filmmakers and networks are in touch with the fact that the complexion of America has changed,\\" said Stephenson Humphries-Brooks, a religion scholar and author of \\"Cinematic Savior: Hollywood\'s Making of the American Christ.\\" \\"A large number of Americans are people of color: Latinos and Middle Easterners and people from India,\\" Humphries-Books continued. \\"That means the audience base is shifting in various and important ways.\\" The audience base may be shifting, but it\'s also tuning in. Each of the Jesus shows drew big ratings, which means you\'ll likely be seeing more of Christ as you channel surf. But according to the Apostle Paul, almost every depiction of Jesus so far has gotten at least one detail wrong: his flowing locks. Real men don\'t wear long hair, said the New Testament scribe.\\n","answer":"In recent years, Jesus has been depicted in various ways in media, reflecting the changing demographics of the audience. Shows like \\"Killing Jesus,\\" \\"A.D.,\\" and \\"Finding Jesus\\" feature actors with diverse backgrounds and appearances, such as Haaz Sleiman, a Muslim actor from Lebanon, and Juan Pablo Di Pace, an Argentinian actor of mixed heritage. This shift towards a more multicultural representation of Jesus reflects the changing complexion of America and the desire for authenticity in historical storytelling. However, these depictions may still fall short of accuracy, as the Bible describes Jesus as having short hair, unlike the long-haired depictions commonly seen in media.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":99},{"index":1,"byte_start":99,"byte_end":173},{"index":2,"byte_start":173,"byte_end":279},{"index":3,"byte_start":279,"byte_end":349},{"index":4,"byte_start":349,"byte_end":478},{"index":5,"byte_start":478,"byte_end":574},{"index":6,"byte_start":574,"byte_end":605},{"index":7,"byte_start":605,"byte_end":634},{"index":8,"byte_start":634,"byte_end":759},{"index":9,"byte_start":759,"byte_end":964},{"index":10,"byte_start":964,"byte_end":1120},{"index":11,"byte_start":1120,"byte_end":1157},{"index":12,"byte_start":1157,"byte_end":1335},{"index":13,"byte_start":1335,"byte_end":1390},{"index":14,"byte_start":1390,"byte_end":1503},{"index":15,"byte_start":1503,"byte_end":1571},{"index":16,"byte_start":1571,"byte_end":1674},{"index":17,"byte_start":1674,"byte_end":1817},{"index":18,"byte_start":1817,"byte_end":2016},{"index":19,"byte_start":2016,"byte_end":2197},{"index":20,"byte_start":2197,"byte_end":2332},{"index":21,"byte_start":2332,"byte_end":2421},{"index":22,"byte_start":2421,"byte_end":2648},{"index":23,"byte_start":2648,"byte_end":2779},{"index":24,"byte_start":2779,"byte_end":2853},{"index":25,"byte_start":2853,"byte_end":2913},{"index":26,"byte_start":2913,"byte_end":3027},{"index":27,"byte_start":3027,"byte_end":3158},{"index":28,"byte_start":3158,"byte_end":3220}],"answer_sentence_indices":[0,1,2,3],"answer_offsets":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":121},{"index":1,"byte_start":121,"byte_end":349},{"index":2,"byte_start":349,"byte_end":517},{"index":3,"byte_start":517,"byte_end":685}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n', 'request': {