rantsGoodForGroups\\":null,\\"RestaurantsReservations\\":null,\\"RestaurantsTakeOut\\":true,\\"WiFi\\":\\"no\\"},\\"business_stars\\":4.5,\\"categories\\":\\"Restaurants, Coffee & Tea, Food\\",\\"city\\":\\"Santa Barbara\\",\\"hours\\":{\\"Friday\\":\\"7:0-18:0\\",\\"Monday\\":\\"7:0-18:0\\",\\"Saturday\\":\\"7:0-18:0\\",\\"Sunday\\":\\"8:0-17:0\\",\\"Thursday\\":\\"7:0-18:0\\",\\"Tuesday\\":\\"7:0-18:0\\",\\"Wednesday\\":\\"7:0-18:0\\"},\\"name\\":\\"Vices & Spices From Around the World\\",\\"review_info\\":[{\\"review_date\\":\\"2022-01-04 20:15:55\\",\\"review_stars\\":5.0,\\"review_text\\":\\"I don\'t go to vices & spices as often as I would imagine given how much I love it but I think that\'s why- I love savoring how good it feels to visit.\\\\n\\\\nThe coffee shop and options have the feel and service of a local coffee bar where everyone remembers you & I love that!\\\\n\\\\nThey do have a wonderful selection of teas, coffee - & even cardamom to sprinkle on your coffee next to the half & half, love that!!\\\\n\\\\nThe store is so cute and always has an interesting selection of gifts and decor for friends or yourself.\\\\n\\\\nI\'ll be back...soon-ish!\\"},{\\"review_date\\":\\"2021-12-27 18:14:17\\",\\"review_stars\\":5.0,\\"review_text\\":\\"They just made me a perfectly steeped cup of tea.  The last time I had a perfect cup of tea from a business was years ago in Seattle. How nice on a rainy day\\"},{\\"review_date\\":\\"2021-12-26 19:04:22\\",\\"review_stars\\":5.0,\\"review_text\\":\\"It\'s cute. It\'s small. It\'s hidden. And it has everything you need for herbs, teas, coffees, cards and other local gifts. There are a couple tables out front, and a few in the back, if you\'d like to enjoy your beverage at the store. Vices&Spices is a true Local favorite located on upper State Street with a hidden parking lot in the back. I found Vices and spices in 2002 and sooooo pleased the shop is still rocking it! I come to Vices & Spices for their coffee beans and fun conversation with staff members. They have a coffee club, so if you buy six pounds of coffee you get one for free. My favorite so far is their Linda\'s blend, comprised of three dark roast coffee beans. They have some specialty coffees available at certain times of year, in particular a 100%Kona coffee from the owner\'s plantation (I think)  in Hawaii. I am a dark or medium roast person, though, so I have tried mostly the dark roasts like the Magic blend. My favorite is still Linda\'s.  If you purchase a few pounds and intend on saving the coffee beans (which I do because I never want to run out of coffee), they offer to specially wrap the beans in plastic to protect them. All staff members are knowledgeable and provide excellent guidance on NOT freezing beans. I find the coffee beans to be of excellent quality. I also like supporting local businesses. While they do sell some baked goods, there aren\'t too many options. I come here for supplies, not typically to sit for a cuppa. I typically see more locals here then students. Definitely a great place for coffee bean and loose leaf tea needs.\\"}],\\"state\\":\\"CA\\"}","answer":"\\"Vices & Spices From Around the World\\" is a highly rated local business in Santa Barbara, CA, offering a variety of foods, coffees, and teas. The establishment opens its doors from 7am to 6pm on weekdays and Saturdays, and from 8am to 5pm on Sundays. The business prides itself on its extensive selection of teas and coffee, including a unique offering of cardamom to sprinkle on your coffee. It also features a range of local gifts and decor items. The shop provides outdoor seating and takeout options, but does not offer Wi-Fi. Customers frequently commend the business for its excellent service and quality products, highlighting the perfectly steeped tea and the high-quality coffee beans, particularly the Linda\'s blend. They also have a coffee club, where if you buy six pounds of coffee, you get one for free. The business doesn\'t have a broad range of baked goods, being more a place for supplies and quick refreshments. Despite its discreet location, it offers a parking lot for the convenience of its customers.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":1337},{"index":1,"byte_start":1337,"byte_end":1420},{"index":2,"byte_start":1420,"byte_end":1528},{"index":3,"byte_start":1528,"byte_end":1540},{"index":4,"byte_start":1540,"byte_end":1553},{"index":5,"byte_start":1553,"byte_end":1639},{"index":6,"byte_start":1639,"byte_end":1750},{"index":7,"byte_start":1750,"byte_end":1857},{"index":8,"byte_start":1857,"byte_end":1939},{"index":9,"byte_start":1939,"byte_end":2028},{"index":10,"byte_start":2028,"byte_end":2110},{"index":11,"byte_start":2110,"byte_end":2197},{"index":12,"byte_start":2197,"byte_end":2348},{"index":13,"byte_start":2348,"byte_end":2453},{"index":14,"byte_start":2453,"byte_end":2484},{"index":15,"byte_start":2484,"byte_end":2674},{"index":16,"byte_start":2674,"byte_end":2764},{"index":17,"byte_start":2764,"byte_end":2816},{"index":18,"byte_start":2816,"byte_end":2857},{"index":19,"byte_start":2857,"byte_end":2925},{"index":20,"byte_start":2925,"byte_end":2985},{"index":21,"byte_start":2985,"byte_end":3033},{"index":22,"byte_start":3033,"byte_end":3116}],"answer_sentence_indices":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7],"answer_offsets":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":142},{"index":1,"byte_start":142,"byte_end":251},{"index":2,"byte_start":251,"byte_end":393},{"index":3,"byte_start":393,"byte_end":450},{"index":4,"byte_start":450,"byte_end":531},{"index":5,"byte_start":531,"byte_end":727},{"index":6,"byte_start":727,"byte_end":818},{"index":7,"byte_start":818,"byte_end":930},{"index":8,"byte_start":930,"byte_end":1022}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n', 'request': {'grammar': 'root ::= r0 "\\n" r1 "\\n" r2 "\\n" r3 "\\n" r4 "\\n" r5 "\\n" r6 "\\n" r7\nr0 ::= "0|" relation "|" probability "|" refs\nr1 ::= "1|" relation "|" probability "|" refs\nr2 ::= "2|" relation